From: Gemini maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: use image plane extents for image attribute bounds

Emulated MTK tiled imports retain their logical pipe_resource dimensions,
while their backing pan_image is a linear array of tiles. After the detiler
reinterprets that array as RGBA8, the logical width is not the image width.
Using it for attribute bounds clips valid image loads: an 80-pixel luma
plane becomes a 20-wide descriptor for a 128-wide tile array.

Derive the image bounds from the selected backing plane, matching its
layout and the sampled texture descriptors. Keep the logical dimensions
for API queries and detile dispatch geometry.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
@@ -2196,8 +2196,16 @@
                                             .tiled_or_linear.surface_stride_B
                                        : rsrc->plane.layout.array_stride_B;
 
-         cfg.s_dimension = u_minify(rsrc->base.width0, level);
-         cfg.t_dimension = u_minify(rsrc->base.height0, level);
+         const struct pan_image_props *props = &rsrc->image.props;
+         unsigned plane_idx = pan_resource_plane_index(rsrc);
+         /* Emulated resources can have a backing extent different from the
+          * logical pipe_resource dimensions. Bounds must match the image. */
+         cfg.s_dimension = u_minify(util_format_get_plane_width(
+                                      props->format, plane_idx,
+                                      props->extent_px.width), level);
+         cfg.t_dimension = u_minify(util_format_get_plane_height(
+                                      props->format, plane_idx,
+                                      props->extent_px.height), level);
          cfg.r_dimension =
             is_3d ? u_minify(rsrc->image.props.extent_px.depth, level)
                   : (image->u.tex.last_layer - image->u.tex.first_layer + 1);
